    isbefore: []  # 5b81
    duplicate_of: []  # 5b81
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 5b81
    pr_ref:  # 5b81
    description: "Discovered via DEEP cohort cohort-001/iter-001 (deep-20260425-210357) on chatwoot. profile.detect_ruby_frameworks correctly identifies Rails from chatwoot's Gemfile (gem 'rails', '~> 7.1'). However, profile.refine_frameworks demotes Rails to dev_frameworks because Ruby app code has zero explicit import edges to the rails gem (Rails autoloads everything via Bundler at boot + convention-based class loading; no .rb file in app code says require 'rails'). enrich_symbols only loads framework patterns from profile.frameworks, not dev_frameworks, so rails.yaml never applies. Concrete consequence on chatwoot: 0 'controller' / 'route' / 'form' / 'serializer' concept tags despite 181 Ruby Controller-named classes (1 of which IS ApplicationController extending ActionController::Base — would match rails.yaml's controller pattern if loaded). 14 classes got the naming-conventions fallback 'controller_by_name' tag. Affects: (a) any Rails app analysis (controller/route/form/serializer concept tagging), (b) downstream linkers that read those tags (controller_routes.py, etc.), (c) bakeoff validation of WI-gudob/WI-gokop on Rails-cohort targets, (d) likely also Phoenix/Elixir (mix-loaded), Django (autoload-by-installed-apps), and other convention-driven frameworks where 'has explicit production import' is a poor proxy for 'is the production framework'. Fix paths: (1) skip refine_frameworks demotion for languages where convention-based loading is the norm (ruby + Gemfile, elixir + mix.exs, etc.); (2) add language-specific evidence beyond import edges (Ruby: presence of config/application.rb with 'class Application < Rails::Application', presence of ApplicationController extending ActionController::Base); (3) merge dev_frameworks into the enrich_symbols input set unconditionally and let the per-pattern symbol_path filter handle the dev/prod scoping. Option (1) is narrowest. Option (3) is broadest but might over-trigger framework patterns on test-only files."  # 5b81
    fields: {}  # 5b81
